Refuse a compressed block of size 0 on the streaming path.

A Compressed_Block always begins with its literals section header (RFC 8878
3.1.1.3.1), so a Block_Size of 0 cannot be one. The one-shot path refuses it
as corrupt (ZSTD_decompressBlock_internal() with srcSize 0), and so does the
zstd CLI. ZSTD_decompressContinue() tested only cBlockSize, so a compressed
block of size 0 took the empty-block branch meant for raw blocks: it ended
the block, and as the last block ended the frame and went on to the
checksum. The same frame was corrupt when decoded whole and a checksum
mismatch, or valid, when streamed (zukomp's fuzz oracle comparing a split
decode with a whole one, #68). An RLE block never reaches the branch: its
cBlockSize is 1.

Written to be upstreamable as-is.

--- a/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
+++ b/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
@@ -1326,6 +1326,13 @@
                 dctx->stage = bp.lastBlock ? ZSTDds_decompressLastBlock : ZSTDds_decompressBlock;
                 return 0;
             }
+            /* Only a raw block can be empty. A compressed block holds at
+             * least its literals section header, so one of size 0 is
+             * corrupt, as ZSTD_decompressBlock_internal() says on the
+             * one-shot path; treating it as empty here ended the block,
+             * or the frame, where that path refuses it. */
+            RETURN_ERROR_IF(bp.blockType == bt_compressed, corruption_detected,
+                            "Empty compressed block");
             /* empty block */
             if (bp.lastBlock) {
